{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\ndef read_ints():\n    return map(int, input().split())\n\ndef first_half(i, cur, n1, a, m, out_set):\n    if i == n1:\n        out_set.add(cur)\n        return\n    first_half(i+1, (cur + a[i]) % m, n1, a, m, out_set)\n    first_half(i+1, cur, n1, a, m, out_set)\n\ndef second_half(i, cur, n, a, m, lst):\n    if i == n:\n        lst.append(cur)\n        return\n    second_half(i+1, (cur + a[i]) % m, n, a, m, lst)\n    second_half(i+1, cur, n, a, m, lst)\n\ndef main():\n    n, m = read_ints()\n    a = list(read_ints())\n    n1 = n // 2\n    a1_set = set()\n    first_half(0, 0, n1, a, m, a1_set)\n    a1 = sorted(a1_set)\n    a2 = []\n    second_half(n1, 0, n, a, m, a2)\n    ans = 0\n    import bisect\n    for x in a2:\n        idx = bisect.bisect_left(a1, m - x)\n        if idx > 0:\n            cand = a1[idx-1] + x\n            if cand > ans:\n                ans = cand\n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static void readInts(Scanner sc, int[] arr) {\n        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {\n            arr[i] = sc.nextInt();\n        }\n    }\n\n    static void firstHalf(int i, int cur, int n1, int[] a, int m, Set<Integer> outSet) {\n        if (i == n1) {\n            outSet.add(cur);\n            return;\n        }\n        firstHalf(i + 1, (cur + a[i]) % m, n1, a, m, outSet);\n        firstHalf(i + 1, cur, n1, a, m, outSet);\n    }\n\n    static void secondHalf(int i, int cur, int n, int[] a, int m, List<Integer> lst) {\n        if (i == n) {\n            lst.add(cur);\n            return;\n        }\n        secondHalf(i + 1, (cur + a[i]) % m, n, a, m, lst);\n        secondHalf(i + 1, cur, n, a, m, lst);\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int m = sc.nextInt();\n        int[] a = new int[n];\n        readInts(sc, a);\n        int n1 = n / 2;\n        Set<Integer> a1Set = new HashSet<>();\n        firstHalf(0, 0, n1, a, m, a1Set);\n        List<Integer> a1 = new ArrayList<>(a1Set);\n        Collections.sort(a1);\n        List<Integer> a2 = new ArrayList<>();\n        secondHalf(n1, 0, n, a, m, a2);\n        int ans = 0;\n        for (int x : a2) {\n            int target = m - x;\n            int idx = Collections.binarySearch(a1, target);\n            if (idx < 0) {\n                idx = -idx - 2; // insertion point - 1\n            } else {\n                // exact match, but we need less than m, so use that index\n                // but if target == 0, then x == m, but x < m, so target > 0\n                // we can use idx directly\n            }\n            if (idx >= 0) {\n                int cand = a1.get(idx) + x;\n                if (cand > ans) {\n                    ans = cand;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(ans);\n        sc.close();\n    }\n}\n</tra